From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: fix SM8150 final counts and cache mappings

The externally captured Test18 log ends immediately after the encoder START
command. LOAD_RESOURCES_DONE was received, but START_DONE and all FTB/ETB
traffic are absent. OUTPUT count was committed during REQBUFS with
host-min 2. The post-control firmware requirements then changed the minimum
to 4.
Mainline programs controls later than Xiaomi's driver, so copying only the
downstream REQBUFS count call creates an invalid lifecycle.

Query final requirements after all encoder controls, route, work mode and
core selection. Commit both external counts from that table, then refresh
internal requirements before LOAD/START. Restore the Test17 property
sequence that reached START_DONE, while retaining zeroed HFI packets.

Test17 also reset after the first ETB. Xiaomi maps Venus buffers with
DMA_ATTR_IOMMU_USE_UPSTREAM_HINT when system cache is present. Carry that
attribute through iommu-dma and select the existing ARM
LPAE 0xf4 MAIR entry. Apply it only to IRIS1 encoder external MMAP buffers
and internal buffers, leaving the working decoder and HFI queues unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
